module

public import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Dimension.Free
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.CurveEulerBridge.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Curves.LinearSeries
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.Reflexive.SpanRestrictInvertible
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.EulerCharAdditivity.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveFromSections.PinnedTwist

/-!
# The morphism to projective space attached to a linear series

[Stacks, Tag 0CCP] says that a `𝔤^r_d` — a linear series `(ℒ, V)` on a nonsingular proper curve
`X` over a field `k`, [Stacks, Tag 0CCN] — gives a morphism `φ : X ⟶ ℙ^r_k` of varieties over `k`
together with a map `α : φ ^* 𝒪(1) ⟶ ℒ` carrying `φ ^* T_0, …, φ ^* T_r` to a basis of `V`.

Its proof has two halves. The first is [Stacks, Tag 01NE]: a family of global sections generating
an invertible module gives a morphism to projective space and a comparison of the twist pinned on
those sections. That half is available here, as
`Stacks.TwistPullbackPinned.exists_hom_over_and_iso_pullback_twistingSheafAtUniverse`. The second
is [Stacks, Tag 0CC4]: a basis `s_0, …, s_r` of `V` need not generate `ℒ`, but on a nonsingular
curve the subsheaf `ℒ' ⊆ ℒ` it *does* generate is again invertible, and the first half applies to
`ℒ'` and then composes with `ℒ' ⟶ ℒ`.

This file does the composition. The second half is isolated as
`Stacks.LinearSeriesMorphism.HasGeneratingInvertibleLift` — a hypothesis for the intermediate
results, so that they hold for an arbitrary family of sections on an arbitrary scheme — and is
then *discharged* for a basis of a linear series on a nonsingular proper curve, which closes
Tag 0CCP.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.LinearSeriesMorphism.HasGeneratingInvertibleLift`: the second half of Tag 0CCP as a
  hypothesis — the family of sections lifts to a family of *generating* sections of an
  *invertible* module mapping to the given one.
* `Stacks.LinearSeriesMorphism.seriesSections`: a family in the chosen space of sections `V` of a
  linear series, read as a family of global sections of the underlying invertible sheaf.

## Main results

* `Stacks.LinearSeriesMorphism.hasGeneratingInvertibleLift_of_generatesStalks`: a generating
  family of sections of an invertible module has a generating invertible lift, so the hypothesis
  below is satisfiable.
* `Stacks.LinearSeriesMorphism.exists_hom_and_hom_pullback_twistingSheafAtUniverse`: for a family
  of global sections with a generating invertible lift there are a morphism `g : X ⟶ ℙ^r_ℤ` and a
  map `α : g ^* 𝒪(1) ⟶ ℒ` with `α (g ^* T_i) = s_i` for every `i`.
* `Stacks.LinearSeriesMorphism.exists_hom_over_and_hom_pullback_twistingSheafAtUniverse`: the
  same over a base scheme, the morphism landing in `ℙ^r_S` and lying over a given `f : X ⟶ S`.
* `Stacks.LinearSeriesMorphism.nonempty_basis`: the chosen space of sections of a linear series of
  dimension `r` has a basis indexed by `Fin (r + 1)`. Unconditional.
* `Stacks.LinearSeriesMorphism.exists_hom_over_and_hom_pullback_twistingSheafAtUniverse_of_basis`:
  the conclusion of Tag 0CCP from the hypothesis above: a morphism `φ : X ⟶ ℙ^r_k` over `k` and a
  map `α : φ ^* 𝒪(1) ⟶ ℒ` carrying `φ ^* T_i` to the chosen basis of `V`.
* `Stacks.LinearSeriesMorphism.seriesSections_ne_zero`: a basis vector of `V` underlies a nonzero
  global section of `ℒ`.
* `Stacks.LinearSeriesMorphism.hasGeneratingInvertibleLift_seriesSections`: **the hypothesis
  above, discharged** for a basis of a linear series on a nonsingular proper curve.
* `Stacks.LinearSeriesMorphism`
  `.exists_hom_over_and_hom_pullback_twistingSheafAtUniverse_of_isRegular`:
  **[Stacks, Tag 0CCP]**, unconditionally.

## Implementation notes

**How the second half is discharged.** Tag 0CC4 is
`AlgebraicGeometry.isTorsionFree_iff_isFiniteLocallyFree` — torsion free is equivalent to finite
locally free for a coherent module on an integral regular scheme of dimension at most one. The
plumbing that feeds it is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ReflexiveModules.isInvertibleModule_spanRestrictModule`: the subsheaf
of `ℒ` generated by finitely many global sections,
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Tag01PFAffineSubsheaf.spanRestrictModule`, is coherent and torsion
free, hence finite locally free, and its rank is one because at the generic point it is a nonzero
subspace of the one-dimensional function-field vector space `ℒ_η`. That the basis sections
generate its stalks is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Tag01PFAffineSubsheaf.generatesStalks_spanRangeSection`, and the
nonvanishing input is `seriesSections_ne_zero` together with injectivity of the germ map at the
generic point on a torsion-free module.

**Nonsingularity is `[IsIntegral X]` together with `IsRegular X`.** Tag 0CCP's hypothesis is that
`X` is a *nonsingular proper curve* over `k`, which is strictly more than what
`AlgebraicGeometry.LinearSeries` carries — properness and `topologicalKrullDim X ≤ 1`. The two
extra hypotheses are exactly what Tag 0CC4 consumes, and they are weaker than the source's: a
nonsingular proper curve over `k` is in particular integral and regular, but separatedness, the
finite type over `k` and dimension exactly one are never used.

**The twist is pulled back along a composite.** The map `α` produced here has source
`(p ≫ projectiveSpaceOver.toIntegralAtUniverse r S) ^* 𝒪(1)`, the pullback along the morphism to
the integral model `ℙ^r_ℤ` underlying `p : X ⟶ ℙ^r_S`, rather than `p ^* 𝒪_{ℙ^r_S}(1)`. The two
are the same sheaf, but identifying them needs the comparison of `(p ≫ q) ^*` with `p ^* ∘ q ^*`
on sheaves of modules, which is not in the repository; this is inherited verbatim from
`Stacks.TwistPullbackPinned.exists_hom_over_and_iso_pullback_twistingSheafAtUniverse` and is
recorded in that file's notes for the same reason.

**`V` is degree-zero cohomology, not `Γ`.** `AlgebraicGeometry.LinearSeries` takes its space of
sections inside `AlgebraicGeometry.cohomologyOverField k f ℒ 0`, which is a right derived functor
and not syntactically `Γ(ℒ, ⊤)`. The passage is
`AlgebraicGeometry.cohomologyOverFieldZeroEquivSections`, a bare `Equiv` and not a `k`-linear
one — `Γ(ℒ, ⊤)` carries no `Module k` instance. So `seriesSections` transports a family rather
than a basis, and the basis stays on the `V` side of the bijection throughout: the statement
asserts that the `α`-images of the pulled-back coordinates are the sections underlying a basis of
`V`, which is Tag 0CCP's "are sent to a basis of `V`".

**The invertibility hypothesis is not a `Mono`.** `HasGeneratingInvertibleLift` asks only for a
map `ℒ' ⟶ ℒ`, not for a subsheaf inclusion, which makes the hypothesis weaker and the results
below correspondingly stronger. Tag 0CC4 delivers the stronger subsheaf form, so nothing is lost.

**The basis is produced, not received.** The unconditional statement existentially quantifies the
basis of `V` rather than taking one as an argument, because Tag 0CCP asserts the existence of
`φ` and `α` for *a* basis; `nonempty_basis` supplies one. The version taking a basis is
`exists_hom_over_and_hom_pullback_twistingSheafAtUniverse_of_basis` composed with
`hasGeneratingInvertibleLift_seriesSections`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CCP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CCP)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CCN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CCN)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CC4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CC4)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NE)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits
open Stacks.AmpleProjectiveImmersion Stacks.ProjectiveFromSections Stacks.TwistPullbackPinned
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Tag01PFAffineSubsheaf

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- **The bijection `H⁰(X, ℱ) ≃ Γ(ℱ, ⊤)` sends `0` to `0`.**
`AlgebraicGeometry.cohomologyOverFieldZeroEquivSections` is a bare `Equiv`, so this does not come
for free from its type; it is read off the naturality statement
`AlgebraicGeometry.cohomologyOverFieldZeroEquivSections_cohomologyOverFieldMap` at the zero
endomorphism of `ℱ`, whose induced map on cohomology is a linear map and therefore kills `0`,
while its action on sections is the zero map. -/
theorem cohomologyOverFieldZeroEquivSections_zero (k : Type u) [Field k] {X : Scheme.{u}}
    (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) (F : X.Modules) :
    cohomologyOverFieldZeroEquivSections k f F 0 = 0 := by
  have h := cohomologyOverFieldZeroEquivSections_cohomologyOverFieldMap k f (0 : F ⟶ F)
    (0 : cohomologyOverField k f F 0)
  rw [map_zero] at h
  refine h.trans ?_
  rw [Scheme.Modules.Hom.zero_app]
  rfl

end AlgebraicGeometry

namespace Stacks.LinearSeriesMorphism

/-- **The second half of [Stacks, Tag 0CCP], as a hypothesis.** A family `s` of
global sections of an `𝒪_X`-module `L` *has a generating invertible lift* if there are an
invertible `𝒪_X`-module `L'`, a map `L' ⟶ L`, and a family of global sections of `L'` which
generates every stalk of `L'` and whose image under that map is `s`.

On a nonsingular proper curve this holds for a basis of a linear series, with `L'` the subsheaf of
`L` generated by the basis: that subsheaf is invertible by [Stacks, Tag 0CC4], which is
`hasGeneratingInvertibleLift_seriesSections` below. -/
def HasGeneratingInvertibleLift {X : Scheme.{u}} (L : X.Modules) {ι : Type*}
    (s : ι → Γ(L, ⊤)) : Prop :=
  ∃ (L' : X.Modules) (_ : Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule X L') (j : L' ⟶ L)
    (s' : ι → Γ(L', ⊤)), GeneratesStalks s' ∧ ∀ i, j.app ⊤ (s' i) = s i

/-- **A generating family of sections of an invertible module has a generating invertible lift**,
namely the identity lift. This is the base-point-free case of [Stacks, Tag 0CCP], in which the
subsheaf generated by the sections is all of `L`; it records that
`HasGeneratingInvertibleLift` is satisfiable and that the hypothesis of the results below is no
stronger than Tag 01NE's in that case. -/
theorem hasGeneratingInvertibleLift_of_generatesStalks {X : Scheme.{u}} {L : X.Modules}
    [Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule X L] {ι : Type*} (s : ι → Γ(L, ⊤))
    (hs : GeneratesStalks s) : HasGeneratingInvertibleLift L s :=
  ⟨L, inferInstance, 𝟙 L, s, hs, fun i => by rw [Scheme.Modules.Hom.id_app]; rfl⟩

/-- Auxiliary form of the next two results, over an arbitrary base scheme. -/
private theorem exists_hom_over_and_hom_pullback_aux {X : Scheme.{u}}
    {L : X.Modules} {n : ℕ} (s : Fin (n + 1) → Γ(L, ⊤)) (hs : HasGeneratingInvertibleLift L s)
    {S : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ S) :
    ∃ p : X ⟶ projectiveSpaceOver n S, p ≫ (projectiveSpaceOver n S ↘ S) = f ∧
      ∃ α : (Scheme.Modules.pullback
          (p ≫ projectiveSpaceOver.toIntegralAtUniverse n S)).obj
            (twistingSheafAtUniverse.{u} n) ⟶ L,
        ∀ i, α.app ⊤ (pullbackCoordSection.{u}
          (p ≫ projectiveSpaceOver.toIntegralAtUniverse n S) i) = s i := by
  obtain ⟨L', hL', j, s', hgen, hj⟩ := hs
  let := hL'
  obtain ⟨p, hp, α, -, hα⟩ :=
    exists_hom_over_and_iso_pullback_twistingSheafAtUniverse s' hgen f
  refine ⟨p, hp, α ≫ j, fun i => ?_⟩
  rw [Scheme.Modules.Hom.comp_app, ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, hα i, hj i]

/-- **A family of global sections with a generating invertible lift gives a morphism to
projective space and a map from the pulled-back twist carrying the coordinates to the family.**
This is the composition of [Stacks, Tag 01NE] with the inclusion of the lift: the pinned
comparison `α' : g ^* 𝒪(1) ≅ L'` of
`Stacks.TwistPullbackPinned.exists_hom_and_iso_pullback_twistingSheafAtUniverse`, followed by
`L' ⟶ L`. The result is only a map, not an isomorphism, which is all Tag 0CCP asserts. -/
theorem exists_hom_and_hom_pullback_twistingSheafAtUniverse {X : Scheme.{u}} {L : X.Modules}
    {n : ℕ} (s : Fin (n + 1) → Γ(L, ⊤)) (hs : HasGeneratingInvertibleLift L s) :
    ∃ (g : X ⟶ projectiveSpaceAtUniverse.{u} n)
      (α : (Scheme.Modules.pullback g).obj (twistingSheafAtUniverse.{u} n) ⟶ L),
      ∀ i, α.app ⊤ (pullbackCoordSection.{u} g i) = s i := by
  obtain ⟨p, -, α, hα⟩ := exists_hom_over_and_hom_pullback_aux s hs (𝟙 X)
  exact ⟨_, α, hα⟩

/-- **The same over a base scheme.** The morphism lands in `ℙ^n_S` and lies over the given
`f : X ⟶ S`, and the twist is pulled back along the underlying morphism to the integral model. -/
theorem exists_hom_over_and_hom_pullback_twistingSheafAtUniverse {X : Scheme.{u}}
    {L : X.Modules} {n : ℕ} (s : Fin (n + 1) → Γ(L, ⊤)) (hs : HasGeneratingInvertibleLift L s)
    {S : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ S) :
    ∃ p : X ⟶ projectiveSpaceOver n S, p ≫ (projectiveSpaceOver n S ↘ S) = f ∧
      ∃ α : (Scheme.Modules.pullback
          (p ≫ projectiveSpaceOver.toIntegralAtUniverse n S)).obj
            (twistingSheafAtUniverse.{u} n) ⟶ L,
        ∀ i, α.app ⊤ (pullbackCoordSection.{u}
          (p ≫ projectiveSpaceOver.toIntegralAtUniverse n S) i) = s i :=
  exists_hom_over_and_hom_pullback_aux s hs f

section LinearSeries

variable {k : Type u} [Field k] {X : Scheme.{u}} {f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)} [IsProper f]
  {hdim : topologicalKrullDim X ≤ 1} {d r : ℕ}

/-- A family in the chosen space of sections `V` of a linear series, read as a family of global
sections of the underlying invertible sheaf through
`AlgebraicGeometry.cohomologyOverFieldZeroEquivSections`. -/
def seriesSections (E : LinearSeries k f hdim d r) {ι : Type*} (v : ι → E.V) :
    ι → Γ(E.L, ⊤) :=
  fun i => cohomologyOverFieldZeroEquivSections k f E.L (v i : cohomologyOverField k f E.L 0)

/-- **The chosen space of sections of a linear series of dimension `r` has a basis indexed by
`Fin (r + 1)`.** Its rank is `r + 1`, which is positive, so the space is finite dimensional and a
basis of that cardinality exists. -/
theorem nonempty_basis (E : LinearSeries k f hdim d r) :
    Nonempty (Module.Basis (Fin (r + 1)) k E.V) := by
  have : Module.Finite k E.V :=
    Module.finite_of_finrank_pos (by rw [E.finrank_eq]; omega)
  exact ⟨Module.finBasisOfFinrankEq k E.V E.finrank_eq⟩

/-- **The conclusion of [Stacks, Tag 0CCP], from the hypothesis isolating its second half.**
For a linear series `(ℒ, V)` of dimension `r` and a basis `b` of `V` whose underlying global
sections have a generating invertible lift, there are a morphism `φ : X ⟶ ℙ^r_k` over `k` and a
map `α : φ ^* 𝒪(1) ⟶ ℒ` sending `φ ^* T_i` to the section underlying `b i`.

The hypothesis `hb` is Tag 0CC4 for this situation; it is discharged for a nonsingular proper
curve by `hasGeneratingInvertibleLift_seriesSections`, and the resulting unconditional statement
is `exists_hom_over_and_hom_pullback_twistingSheafAtUniverse_of_isRegular`. -/
theorem exists_hom_over_and_hom_pullback_twistingSheafAtUniverse_of_basis
    (E : LinearSeries k f hdim d r) (b : Module.Basis (Fin (r + 1)) k E.V)
    (hb : HasGeneratingInvertibleLift E.L (seriesSections E b)) :
    ∃ p : X ⟶ projectiveSpaceOver r (Spec (.of k)),
      p ≫ (projectiveSpaceOver r (Spec (.of k)) ↘ Spec (.of k)) = f ∧
      ∃ α : (Scheme.Modules.pullback
          (p ≫ projectiveSpaceOver.toIntegralAtUniverse r (Spec (.of k)))).obj
            (twistingSheafAtUniverse.{u} r) ⟶ E.L,
        ∀ i, α.app ⊤ (pullbackCoordSection.{u}
          (p ≫ projectiveSpaceOver.toIntegralAtUniverse r (Spec (.of k))) i) =
          seriesSections E b i :=
  exists_hom_over_and_hom_pullback_twistingSheafAtUniverse (seriesSections E b) hb f

/-- **A basis of the chosen space of sections of a linear series underlies a nonzero global
section.** The passage from degree-zero cohomology to global sections is a bijection sending `0`
to `0`, so it carries the nonzero vector `b i` to a nonzero section. -/
theorem seriesSections_ne_zero (E : LinearSeries k f hdim d r)
    (b : Module.Basis (Fin (r + 1)) k E.V) (i : Fin (r + 1)) : seriesSections E b i ≠ 0 := by
  intro h0
  refine b.ne_zero i (Submodule.coe_eq_zero.mp
    ((cohomologyOverFieldZeroEquivSections k f E.L).injective ?_))
  exact h0.trans (cohomologyOverFieldZeroEquivSections_zero k f E.L).symm

/-- **The hypothesis of [Stacks, Tag 0CC4] for a basis of a linear series on a nonsingular proper
curve.** The subsheaf of `ℒ` generated by the sections underlying the basis is invertible, the
basis sections generate its stalks, and it maps to `ℒ` by the inclusion — which is exactly a
generating invertible lift.

Invertibility of that subsheaf is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ReflexiveModules.isInvertibleModule_spanRestrictModule`, Tag 0CC4 in
the shape this proof needs it; stalk generation is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Tag01PFAffineSubsheaf.generatesStalks_spanRangeSection`. The
nonvanishing input the former needs is `seriesSections_ne_zero` together with injectivity of the
germ map at the generic point on a torsion-free module. -/
theorem hasGeneratingInvertibleLift_seriesSections [IsIntegral X] (hreg : IsRegular X)
    (E : LinearSeries k f hdim d r) (b : Module.Basis (Fin (r + 1)) k E.V) :
    HasGeneratingInvertibleLift E.L (seriesSections E b) := by
  have hnoeth : IsLocallyNoetherian X :=
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CurveEulerBridge.isLocallyNoetherian_of_isProper_over_field k f
  have hinv : Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule X E.L := E.isInvertible
  have hqc : E.L.IsQuasicoherent :=
    Stacks.AmpleGlobalGeneration.isQuasicoherent_of_isInvertibleModule E.L
  have hgerm :=
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ReflexiveModules.Γgerm_genericPoint_ne_zero_of_ne_zero E.L
      (seriesSections_ne_zero E b 0)
  exact ⟨spanRestrictModule E.L (Set.range (seriesSections E b)),
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ReflexiveModules.isInvertibleModule_spanRestrictModule E.L hreg
      hdim (seriesSections E b) (Set.finite_range _) hgerm,
    spanRestrictSubsheafι E.L (Set.range (seriesSections E b)),
    spanRangeSection E.L (seriesSections E b),
    generatesStalks_spanRangeSection E.L (seriesSections E b),
    fun i => app_spanRestrictSubsheafι_spanRangeSection E.L (seriesSections E b) i⟩

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0CCP.** Let `k` be a field, `X` a nonsingular proper curve over `k` and
`(ℒ, V)` a `𝔤^r_d` on `X`. Then there are a morphism `φ : X ⟶ ℙ^r_k` of varieties over `k` — a
morphism lying over the structure morphism of `X` — and a map `α : φ ^* 𝒪(1) ⟶ ℒ` carrying
`φ ^* T_0, …, φ ^* T_r` to a basis of `V`.

Nonsingularity enters as integrality of `X` together with `hreg`; the properness and the
dimension bound are carried by `AlgebraicGeometry.LinearSeries`. The basis is the one supplied by
`nonempty_basis`, and the conclusion asserts that the `α`-images of the pulled-back coordinates
are the sections underlying it, which is the source's "are sent to a basis of `V`". -/
@[stacks 0CCP]
theorem exists_hom_over_and_hom_pullback_twistingSheafAtUniverse_of_isRegular [IsIntegral X]
    (hreg : IsRegular X) (E : LinearSeries k f hdim d r) :
    ∃ (b : Module.Basis (Fin (r + 1)) k E.V) (p : X ⟶ projectiveSpaceOver r (Spec (.of k))),
      p ≫ (projectiveSpaceOver r (Spec (.of k)) ↘ Spec (.of k)) = f ∧
      ∃ α : (Scheme.Modules.pullback
          (p ≫ projectiveSpaceOver.toIntegralAtUniverse r (Spec (.of k)))).obj
            (twistingSheafAtUniverse.{u} r) ⟶ E.L,
        ∀ i, α.app ⊤ (pullbackCoordSection.{u}
          (p ≫ projectiveSpaceOver.toIntegralAtUniverse r (Spec (.of k))) i) =
          seriesSections E b i := by
  obtain ⟨b⟩ := nonempty_basis E
  exact ⟨b, exists_hom_over_and_hom_pullback_twistingSheafAtUniverse_of_basis E b
    (hasGeneratingInvertibleLift_seriesSections hreg E b)⟩

end LinearSeries

end Stacks.LinearSeriesMorphism

end
